<h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
<p>These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of The H.E.L.P. System (the "Service"), a software-as-a-service platform operated by <span class="placeholder">[LEGAL ENTITY NAME — e.g., H.E.L.P. Center LLC, or "Joy Watford d/b/a H.E.L.P. Center"]</span> ("H.E.L.P. Center," "we," "us," or "our"). By accessing the Service, creating an account, or paying for a subscription, you agree to be bound by these Terms and our Privacy Policy. If you do not agree to these Terms, you may not use the Service.</p>

<h2>2. Description of Service</h2>
<p>The H.E.L.P. System is a multi-tenant business management platform designed for coaches, faith-based leaders, women entrepreneurs, side-hustlers, and other everyday leaders ("Users") to manage clients, bookings, revenue, documents, and content from a single dashboard. The Service includes optional integrations with third-party providers including Groq (AI), Resend (email), Stripe (payments), and SignFlow or DocuSeal-compatible providers (e-signature).</p>

<h2>3. Eligibility and Account Registration</h2>
<p>You must be at least 18 years old and capable of entering into a legally binding agreement to use the Service. You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your login credentials and for all activity that occurs under your account. You agree to notify us immediately at <span class="placeholder">[SUPPORT EMAIL]</span> of any unauthorized access or breach.</p>

<h2>4. Subscription Plans and Billing</h2>

<h3>4.1 Plans</h3>
<p>The Service is offered on monthly recurring subscriptions:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Solo — $29.99 per month</strong> with a 7-day free trial</li>
  <li><strong>Pro — $59.99 per month</strong> with a 7-day free trial</li>
</ul>
<p>Pricing may change with at least 30 days' written notice. Existing subscriptions will continue at the current price until your next renewal after the notice period expires.</p>

<h3>4.2 Billing</h3>
<p>Payments are processed by Stripe, Inc. You authorize us to charge your provided payment method on a recurring monthly basis for the applicable subscription tier. You are responsible for keeping your payment method current. If a payment fails, the Service may be suspended after a reasonable retry period.</p>

<h3>4.3 Taxes</h3>
<p>You are responsible for all applicable sales, use, or value-added taxes. Where required, we will collect and remit tax via Stripe Tax.</p>

<h2>5. Free Trial</h2>
<p>New accounts receive a 7-day free trial of the selected plan. No charge is made during the trial. You may cancel at any time during the trial to avoid being charged. After the trial ends, your subscription automatically converts to a paid monthly subscription at the price of the selected tier. Trials are limited to one per person and one per payment method.</p>

<h2>6. Cancellation and Refunds</h2>

<h3>6.1 Cancellation</h3>
<p>You may cancel your subscription at any time through your account settings or by emailing <span class="placeholder">[SUPPORT EMAIL]</span>. Cancellation takes effect at the end of your current billing period. You will retain access to the Service through the end of the period for which you have paid.</p>

<h3>6.2 Refunds</h3>
<p>If you are dissatisfied with the Service, you may request a refund within <strong>14 days</strong> of your <em>first</em> paid charge (after the free trial). Refunds are issued at our discretion and are not guaranteed for cause unrelated to a material defect of the Service. Beyond this 14-day window, all charges are non-refundable. Partial-month refunds are not provided.</p>

